From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: stop WFDMA before freeing ring buffers on
 reset

mt7915_dma_reset() frees the tx and rx queue buffers before it disables
WFDMA, and on a full reset after a firmware crash or MCU timeout nothing
has stopped the engine yet on MT7986 (interrupts are only masked for
PCIe devices). Rx DMA that is still running can then write into pages
already returned to the allocator.

Disable WFDMA and give it a moment to settle first, as
mt7996_dma_reset() does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/dma.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/dma.c b/mt7915/dma.c
index aabd3736..dd39fbad 100644
--- a/mt7915/dma.c
+++ b/mt7915/dma.c
@@ -593,6 +593,12 @@ int mt7915_dma_reset(struct mt7915_dev *dev, bool force)
 	struct mtk_wed_device *wed = &dev->mt76.mmio.wed;
 	int i;
 
+	/* On a full reset nothing has stopped WFDMA yet: stop it before
+	 * freeing the buffers its descriptors still point to.
+	 */
+	mt7915_dma_disable(dev, false);
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
 	/* clean up hw queues */
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->mt76.phy.q_tx); i++) {
 		mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[i], true);
